Scaling Jenkins with Distributed Build Agents
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the concept of distributed builds in Jenkins
Configure Jenkins master-agent architecture on a single machine
Set up multiple Jenkins agent nodes using different connection methods
Distribute build workloads across multiple agents for parallel execution
Monitor and manage distributed builds through the Jenkins interface
Troubleshoot common issues with Jenkins agent connectivity
Optimize build performance through proper agent configuration
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Jenkins fundamentals
Familiarity with Linux command line operations
Knowledge of basic networking concepts
Understanding of SSH key authentication
Experience with Jenkins job configuration
Basic knowledge of Java applications
